a0084187e2b229fb179220102672cab4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Malnati/node-gen/commits/bc8d3fda0084187e2b229fb179220102672cab4d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35036961?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Malnati/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Malnati/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Malnati/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Malnati/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Malnati","id":35036961,"login":"Malnati","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MDM2OTYx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Malnati/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Malnati/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Malnati/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Malnati/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Malnati/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Malnati","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Malnati/node-gen/commits/da13b3486b04366f90372efa145a143edb0f8141/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-22T21:46:38Z","email":"35036961+Malnati@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ricardo Malnati"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-22T21:46:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Enhance E2E testing documentation and generator mock script (#212)\n\n* Enhance E2E testing documentation and generator mock script\n\n- Updated README.md to clarify the E2E testing environment setup, including details on database types and health checks.\n- Refactored run.js in the E2E generator mock to improve database connectivity checks and ensure only allowed database types are processed.\n- Enhanced logging messages for better clarity during E2E tests, including coverage details for endpoints and database verifications.\n- Adjusted timeout settings for health checks and completion loops to optimize testing performance.\n\nThese changes aim to improve the usability and reliability of the E2E testing framework, ensuring comprehensive validation across supported database types.\n\n* Implement MSSQL support in DataSourceService and enhance E2E testing scripts\n\n- Added support for MSSQL database type in DataSourceService, allowing dynamic configuration based on environment variables.\n- Updated service.ejs template to improve transaction handling, ensuring proper entity retrieval and saving.\n- Modified E2E generator mock scripts to reflect changes in database structure, including updates to the selling project and the introduction of a new Google Calendar mock database.\n- Enhanced SQL initialization scripts for MySQL to include new tables for Google Calendar integration, improving overall database structure and testing capabilities.\n\nThese changes aim to enhance database support and improve the reliability of the E2E testing framework.\n\n* Refactor service.ejs template to enhance primary key handling\n\n- Updated the logic for retrieving the primary key in the service.ejs template, improving clarity and ensuring proper entity retrieval.\n- Introduced a variable for the primary key column to streamline the code and enhance readability.\n\nThese changes aim to improve the maintainability and reliability of the service generation process.\n\n* Enhance primary key handling and logging in service.ejs template\n\n- Updated the service.ejs template to improve primary key retrieval logic, ensuring that the primary key defaults to \"id\" when not explicitly defined.\n- Enhanced logging messages to reflect the updated primary key handling, improving clarity during entity operations.\n- Streamlined the transaction logic for entity insertion and retrieval, enhancing overall code readability and maintainability.\n\nThese changes aim to improve the reliability and clarity of the service generation process.\n\n* Refactor primary key handling in ServiceGenerator for improved clarity\n\n- Updated the logic for determining primary key columns in the ServiceGenerator, enhancing the clarity and reliability of primary key retrieval.\n- Introduced a more streamlined approach to check for single primary key columns, improving code readability and maintainability.\n\nThese changes aim to enhance the robustness of the service generation process by ensuring accurate primary key identification.\n\n* Add E2E cleanup target and update MySQL initialization scripts\n\n- Introduced a new `e2e-clean` target in the Makefile to remove E2E containers and volumes, facilitating a fresh initialization of the database.\n- Updated the Docker Compose configuration to change the MySQL initialization script path, ensuring the correct database schema is loaded.\n- Increased the wait time for MySQL readiness checks in the entrypoint script to improve reliability during E2E tests.\n- Enhanced error logging in the E2E generator mock script to provide guidance for resolving common MySQL access issues.\n\nThese changes aim to streamline the E2E testing process and improve database initialization reliability.\n\n* Refactor primary key definitions in SQL Server DDL files for clarity\n\n- Updated the primary key definitions in the `tb_order_line` and `tb_simple_item_tag` tables to use explicit constraint names, enhancing readability and maintainability of the database schema.\n- Removed redundant primary key definitions to streamline the table structure.\n\nThese changes aim to improve the clarity and consistency of the database schema across projects.\n\n* Refactor primary key constraint in tb_order_line table for clarity\n\n- Updated the primary key definition in the `tb_order_line` table to use an explicit constraint name, improving readability and maintainability of the database schema.\n- Removed redundant primary key definition to streamline the table structure.\n\nThese changes aim to enhance the clarity and consistency of the database schema.\n\n* Enhance database schema handling and DTO generation\n\n- Updated the `DbReaderMysql` and `DbReaderSqlServer` classes to include identity column detection, improving support for auto-increment fields.\n- Refactored the `DTOGenerator`, `InterfaceGenerator`, and `ServiceGenerator` classes to streamline the handling of table structures, ensuring consistent access to columns and relations.\n- Modified the `generateDTOContent`, `generateInterfaceContent`, and related methods to accept a `Table` object, enhancing clarity and maintainability.\n- Improved the handling of optional properties in DTOs, particularly for external IDs, to ensure accurate data representation.\n\nThese changes aim to enhance the robustness and clarity of the database interaction and data transfer processes.\n\n* Update ServiceGenerator and E2E mock script for improved entity handling\n\n- Modified the `ServiceGenerator` to correctly assign relation names, enhancing the clarity of entity relationships.\n- Updated the expected project structure in the E2E generator mock script to reflect changes in table and module names, ensuring consistency with the current database schema.\n\nThese changes aim to improve the accuracy of entity generation and testing processes.\n\n* Enhance environment configuration and E2E mock script for improved reliability\n\n- Updated the `EnvGenerator` to handle optional database configuration properties, ensuring defaults are set for missing values.\n- Modified the `ServiceGenerator` to safely access relation properties, preventing potential runtime errors.\n- Enhanced the E2E mock script to support unique external IDs and added a mechanism to skip API start for specific database types, improving testing flexibility.\n\nThese changes aim to increase the robustness and reliability of the environment setup and testing processes.\n\n* Update package.json scripts and enhance E2E generator mock for improved build process\n\n- Changed `nest` commands to use `npx` for better compatibility and execution.\n- Enhanced the E2E generator mock script to set the `DATABASE_PATH` for SQLite connections, improving environment configuration.\n- Improved error handling during the npm install process in the E2E mock script to provide clearer feedback on failures.\n\nThese changes aim to streamline the build process and enhance the reliability of the E2E testing environment.\n\n* Enhance E2E mock script and environment configuration for improved testing\n\n- Updated the E2E mock script to include support for multiple database types, enhancing flexibility in testing scenarios.\n- Improved error handling and logging in the E2E mock script to provide clearer feedback during execution.\n- Refined environment configuration to ensure consistent setup across different testing environments.\n\nThese changes aim to streamline the E2E testing process and improve overall reliability.\n\n* Update E2E mock database configurations and initialization scripts\n\n- Changed database names from *_mock to * for consistency across MySQL, PostgreSQL, and SQL Server configurations.\n- Updated initialization scripts and connection settings to reflect the new database names, ensuring proper setup during E2E tests.\n- Enhanced logging messages in the entrypoint script to provide clearer feedback on database readiness and initialization status.\n\nThese changes aim to streamline the E2E testing process and improve the clarity of database configurations.\n\n* Update E2E generator mock project structure for enhanced entity management\n\n- Refactored the expected project structure in the E2E generator mock to include a comprehensive list of projects, tables, module names, and entity files.\n- Added new project configurations for accounts, addresses, auth, communications, and more, ensuring alignment with the current database schema.\n- This update aims to improve the accuracy and clarity of entity generation during E2E testing processes.\n\n* Update E2E testing configuration to enhance database handling and flexibility\n\n- Modified the entrypoint script to clarify the use of `E2E_DB_TYPES`, indicating it now only affects the initial container checks, not the test matrix.\n- Updated README files to reflect changes in how database connection files are discovered and utilized, ensuring all available connections are tested.\n- Improved logging in the E2E mock script to provide clearer feedback on the database types being utilized during testing.\n\nThese changes aim to streamline the E2E testing process and improve the accuracy of database interactions.\n\n* Refactor E2E generator mock to enhance project structure and post-verification handling\n\n- Removed the previous static `E2E_POST_VERIFY` configuration and integrated post-verification logic directly into the `PROJECT_EXPECTED` structure for each project.\n- Updated the structure to include detailed post-verification specifications, improving clarity and alignment with the current database schema.\n- These changes aim to streamline the E2E testing process and enhance the accuracy of database interactions during verification.\n\n* Refactor E2E generator structure and update database paths\n\n- Renamed and reorganized paths in the E2E generator to replace references from `e2e-generator-mock` to `e2e-generator`, ensuring consistency across the project.\n- Updated `.dockerignore`, `.gitignore`, and various scripts to reflect the new directory structure for database files and initialization scripts.\n- Enhanced README documentation to guide users on the updated project structure and usage instructions.\n\nThese changes aim to streamline the E2E testing process and improve clarity in project organization.\n\n* Update E2E generator database initialization paths for consistency\n\n- Changed the database initialization script path for the schedule project from `init.mysql.sql` to `database.mysql.sql` to align with the updated project structure.\n- This update ensures consistency in database file references across the E2E testing environment.\n\n* Update E2E generator database initialization scripts for schedule project\n\n- Changed the database initialization script for the schedule project to use separate files for schema and data, enhancing clarity and organization.\n- Added a `USE todo;` statement in the selling project''s initialization script to ensure the correct database context is set during E2E tests.\n\nThese updates aim to improve the structure and accuracy of database initialization in the E2E testing environment.\n\n* Update E2E generator to include schedule project in database initialization\n\n- Added the schedule project to the PostgreSQL and SQL Server initialization scripts, ensuring its database and schema are created correctly.\n- Updated README documentation to reflect the inclusion of the schedule project and clarify the structure of database references.\n- Enhanced MySQL initialization scripts to grant privileges for the schedule database, ensuring proper access during E2E tests.\n\nThese changes aim to improve the completeness and accuracy of the E2E testing environment.\n\n* Refactor E2E database initialization scripts for improved project discovery\n\n- Removed hardcoded volume mappings in the Docker Compose file for MySQL, allowing for dynamic project discovery during initialization.\n- Enhanced the PostgreSQL and SQL Server initialization scripts to automatically discover and apply schemas for projects based on their directory structure.\n- Updated the entrypoint script to provide clearer logging during MySQL initialization, indicating when databases are being set up.\n\nThese changes aim to streamline the E2E testing process by improving the flexibility and maintainability of database initialization.\n\n* Refactor E2E database initialization and update documentation\n\n- Removed hardcoded database initialization scripts for MySQL and PostgreSQL, enhancing dynamic project discovery.\n- Updated the entrypoint script to improve logging during PostgreSQL readiness checks.\n- Revised README files to reflect changes in database initialization processes and clarify the structure of the E2E testing environment.\n- Deleted obsolete MySQL initialization scripts for projects, streamlining the setup process.\n\nThese changes aim to enhance the flexibility and maintainability of the E2E testing environment.\n\n* Enhance SQL Server initialization to support batch processing of DDL statements\n\n- Introduced a new function to split SQL Server DDL content into batches using the ''GO'' statement, improving the execution of multiple statements.\n- Updated the main initialization logic to process each batch individually, ensuring better handling of complex schema definitions.\n\nThese changes aim to improve the robustness and flexibility of the E2E database initialization process.\n\n* Refactor SQL Server DDL for tb_booking_participant table\n\n- Added a named constraint for the primary key on the tb_booking_participant table to improve clarity and maintainability.\n- Removed redundant primary key declaration to streamline the DDL structure.\n\nThese changes enhance the organization of the database schema and ensure better adherence to SQL Server best practices.\n\n* Update SQL Server DDL and data insertion for transaction table\n\n- Renamed the ''transaction'' table to use square brackets for compatibility with SQL Server syntax.\n- Updated the INSERT statements to reflect the new table name format, ensuring consistency in database operations.\n\nThese changes enhance the clarity and correctness of the SQL scripts used in the E2E testing environment.\n\n* Update postVerify configuration in E2E generator to correct code value\n\n- Changed the ''code'' value in the postVerify configuration for the ''country'' table from ''E2E'' to ''E2'' to ensure accurate verification during E2E tests.\n\nThis update aims to enhance the correctness of the E2E testing process.\n\n* Enhance table name extraction in SQL Server DDL processing\n\n- Updated the regular expression used to extract the first table name from SQL Server DDL content to support both square bracket and standard naming conventions.\n- Modified the `getFirstTableName` function to return the correct table name format, improving compatibility with various SQL Server table definitions.\n\nThese changes aim to enhance the robustness of the E2E generator''s SQL parsing capabilities.\n\n* Add MySQL user creation and privilege flushing in E2E generator\n\n- Implemented user creation for the MySQL database during initialization, ensuring that the E2E user is properly escaped to prevent SQL injection issues.\n- Added a command to flush privileges after user creation to apply changes immediately.\n\nThese enhancements improve the security and functionality of the E2E testing environment for MySQL.\n\n* Add Git repository initialization in main generator script\n\n- Introduced a new function to ensure the output directory is initialized as a Git repository, including commands to add and commit files.\n- Updated the main function to call this new Git initialization function, enhancing version control capabilities for generated projects.\n\nThese changes aim to improve the management and tracking of generated project files within a Git repository.\n\n* Update SQL scripts to use quoted table name for ''transaction''\n\n- Modified the DDL and SQL files to use double quotes around the ''transaction'' table name for consistency and to prevent potential conflicts with SQL reserved keywords.\n- Ensured that the INSERT statements reflect this change, maintaining compatibility with the database schema.\n\nThese updates enhance the clarity and correctness of the SQL scripts used in the E2E testing environment.\n\n* Add Git user configuration during repository initialization\n\n- Updated the main generator script to configure Git user email and name upon repository initialization, ensuring proper attribution for commits.\n- Enhanced the Git setup process to improve version control practices for generated projects.\n\nThese changes aim to streamline the management of generated project files within a Git repository.","tree":{"sha":"56f6b87d29ae6c27e9a9b85441bdbf49957139d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Malnati/node-gen/git/trees/56f6b87d29ae6c27e9a9b85441bdbf49957139d6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Malnati/node-gen/git/commits/da13b3486b04366f90372efa145a143edb0f8141","verification":{"payload":"tree 56f6b87d29ae6c27e9a9b85441bdbf49957139d6\nparent 0bf62797d1ade742390165610ea418a9d7f8f2cb\nauthor Ricardo Malnati <35036961+Malnati@users.noreply.github.com> 1771796798 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1771796798 -0300\n\nEnhance E2E testing documentation and generator mock script (#212)\n\n* Enhance E2E testing documentation and generator mock script\n\n- Updated README.md to clarify the E2E testing environment setup, including details on database types and health checks.\n- Refactored run.js in the E2E generator mock to improve database connectivity checks and ensure only allowed database types are processed.\n- Enhanced logging messages for better clarity during E2E tests, including coverage details for endpoints and database verifications.\n- Adjusted timeout settings for health checks and completion loops to optimize testing performance.\n\nThese changes aim to improve the usability and reliability of the E2E testing framework, ensuring comprehensive validation across supported database types.\n\n* Implement MSSQL support in DataSourceService and enhance E2E testing scripts\n\n- Added support for MSSQL database type in DataSourceService, allowing dynamic configuration based on environment variables.\n- Updated service.ejs template to improve transaction handling, ensuring proper entity retrieval and saving.\n- Modified E2E generator mock scripts to reflect changes in database structure, including updates to the selling project and the introduction of 