https://api.github.com/users/Malnati","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Malnati/node-gen/commits/dae2a6bf3eded5d21f602ac3b18ebf9672526d1c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-20T20:16:13Z","email":"35036961+Malnati@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ricardo Malnati"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-20T20:16:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Refactor database schema for selling project to improve structure and… (#209)\n\n* Refactor database schema for selling project to improve structure and integrity\n\n- Renamed ''sale'' table to ''tb_order'' and ''sale_item'' table to ''tb_order_line'' for clarity.\n- Updated fields in ''tb_order'' to include ''discount'' and ''ordered_at'', and made ''external_id'' unique.\n- Enhanced ''tb_order_line'' with ''line_total'' and established foreign key relationships with ''tb_order''.\n- Ensured consistency in data types and constraints across MySQL initialization and schema files.\n\nThese changes aim to enhance the relational integrity and clarity of the database structure for the selling project.\n\n* Refactor payment and currency schema for improved data integrity\n\n- Removed the ''currency'' table from the database schema across MySQL, PostgreSQL, SQLite, and SQL Server, simplifying the payment structure.\n- Updated the ''payment'' table to change ''currency_id'' from INT to CHAR(36) for better alignment with external identifiers.\n- Modified SQL insert statements to directly reference currency codes instead of IDs, enhancing clarity and reducing complexity in data handling.\n\nThese changes aim to streamline the payment processing system and improve the overall integrity of the database structure.","tree":{"sha":"af9c1ae9e10feedce6b6f012962ac2dbbaf1220d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Malnati/node-gen/git/trees/af9c1ae9e10feedce6b6f012962ac2dbbaf1220d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Malnati/node-gen/git/commits/dae2a6bf3eded5d2