ed SQL scripts for MySQL, PostgreSQL, SQLite, and SQL Server to incorporate the new schema, ensuring consistency across different database types.\n- Improved documentation and comments within the schema files to clarify the purpose and relationships of the new tables.\n\nThese changes aim to enhance the robustness and flexibility of the E2E testing framework and improve the overall database structure for the selling project.\n\n* Enhance booking schema and participant association in database\n\n- Added ''organizer_account_id'' to the ''tb_booking'' table to reference the organizer of the booking.\n- Updated ''tb_booking_participant'' table to replace ''participant_id'' with ''account_id'', improving clarity in participant associations.\n- Modified SQL insert statements across MySQL, PostgreSQL, SQLite, and SQL Server to reflect the new schema changes, ensuring consistency in data handling.\n\nThese updates aim to improve the relational integrity and clarity of the booking and participant data structure.","tree":{"sha":"bbacd5e0cb412708c383a3c37810c4b926ad190b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Malnati/node-gen/git/trees/bbacd5e0cb412708c383a3c37810c4b926ad190b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Malnati/node-gen/git/commits/53d485248f9e26ee655ea3a299dd3aa915530483","verification":{"payload":"tree bbacd5e0cb412708c383a3c37810c4b926ad190b\nparent 325c937f944b6db27ef9eb82791e909607590f4b\nauthor Ricardo Malnati <35036961+Malnati@users.noreply.github.com> 1771616539 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1771616539 -0300\n\nRefactor database schema for selling project and enhance E2E testing … (#208)\n\n* Refactor database schema for selling project and enhance E2E testing setup\n\n- Updated the DATA_DICTIONARY.md to reflect the new schema version (1–26) and detailed changes in the selling project, including the introduction of new tables (tb_customer, tb_payment_method, tb_order, tb_order_line, tb_payment, tb_stock_movement, tb_customer_address) with improved relational integrity and data structure.\n- Modified init-postgres.js and init-sqlserver.js to align with the new table names and ensure proper database initialization during E2E tests.\n- Enhanced SQL scripts for MySQL, PostgreSQL, SQLite, and SQL Server to incorporate the new schema, ensuring consistency across different database types.\n- Improved documentation and comments within the schema files to clarify the purpose and relationships of the new tables.\n\nThese changes aim to enhance the robustness and flexibility of the E2E testing framework and improve the overall database structure for the selling project.\n\n* Enhance booking schema and participant association in database\n\n- Added ''organizer_account_id'' to the ''tb_booking'' table to reference the organizer of the booking.\n- Updated ''tb_booking_participant'' table to replace ''participant_id'' with ''account_id'', improving clarity in participant associations.\n- Modified SQL insert statements across MySQL, PostgreSQL, SQLite, and SQL Server to reflect the new schema changes, ensuring consistency in data handling.\n\nThese updates aim to improve the relational integrity and clarity of the booking and participant data structure.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpmLkbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7YEQABda8lY2En2tDMX/eC3NS+d3\nIXIKp8mnQx6CgXPHm/zdjRXm77EKTND18u3dtVev42W+a09MR2nNLE3PQclb8UWt\nZsQqD+tOvzhPLalxSv3MGT1cqsKLFkSbh7s4FSg98IUA6qc0okmx8NI9/PAFAdhl\n6GiU7ckb6rW1W4E1XPxwiJWMe+5gthUCP1qPa95si8jah4l42q0SE5iodGuy1h6p\nNX8rf8zwkRHsayvlJ5HEWclq/0JA34UXMxholBSiTFhFR1kHJjrYNx2kaM2sBKPb\nGjP67Tcm2e8mvDoN8NzqJDBTiBpt0H5LwKhS+ZnqzZCww1vrg67Mz7/B8bLprR77\nSGZAlKrIz16ndaUcUoBhaic4Bi2AYdfLC/lJy5I4TnT0GwaY0VANxm877Up/2gLk\nZ07k6ckU/vGmXB4Rn29AFKctBnnJ2Yma+srF/e2BaOXULWklflX9/ZnlA2HxOiMl\nXZOh+R5+nczMlUj2MVowLOL6A0L30kY7TYaixjRBkYUL+aU3FzWhEJgnB2Ux2XMp\nALTy9G+GdrTMysxeqF+4rKaRSnY1FtmqICt/hEMv2yQKTATEdwb7u4BNZDGgXWOJ\npjwmA/G6QHPIEadLK9nptcLVC4P9j/VJWqONC7I1thm8onZ6Pnps93zrh+lZS