i/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Malnati","id":35036961,"login":"Malnati","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MDM2OTYx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Malnati/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Malnati/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Malnati/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Malnati/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Malnati/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Malnati","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Malnati/node-gen/commits/325c937f944b6db27ef9eb82791e909607590f4b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-20T18:49:08Z","email":"35036961+Malnati@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ricardo Malnati"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-20T18:49:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Enhance E2E testing setup with improved database support and document… (#207)\n\n* Enhance E2E testing setup with improved database support and documentation updates\n\n- Updated Docker Compose configuration to include additional database types and health checks, enhancing testing versatility.\n- Refactored E2E generator mock script to improve database connectivity checks and streamline testing processes.\n- Revised documentation to clarify new setup instructions and database connection handling, ensuring better usability for developers.\n\nThese changes aim to improve the robustness and flexibility of the E2E testing framework for the code generator.\n\n* Enhance database schema for accounts, addresses, contacts, payments, and users\n\n- Added ''tenant'' and ''account_id'' fields to the ''account'', ''address'', ''contact'', ''payment_method'', and ''app_user'' tables across MySQL, PostgreSQL, SQLite, and SQL Server schemas.\n- Updated corresponding SQL insert statements to include ''tenant'' and ''account_id'' for data consistency and relational integrity.\n\nThese changes aim to improve the structure and relational mapping of the database, facilitating better multi-tenancy support and data organization.\n\n* Enhance database schema for payments and users by adding contact_id field\n\n- Added ''contact_id'' field to the ''payment_method'' and ''app_user'' tables across MySQL, PostgreSQL, SQLite, and SQL Server schemas.\n- Updated corresponding SQL insert statements to include ''contact_id'' for improved data relationships and integrity.\n\nThese changes aim to enhance the relational structure of the database, supporting better data management and multi-tenancy capabilities.\n\n* Refactor payment schema to enhance data integrity and structure\n\n- Updated the ''payment'' table schema across MySQL, PostgreSQL, SQLite, and SQL Server to include an ''external_id'' field for better identification.\n- Modified the SQL insert statements to incorporate ''external_id'', ''billing_address_id'', ''method'', ''amount'', ''currency_code'', and ''status'' fields, improving the relational mapping and data management.\n- Added a check constraint for the ''method'' field to ensure valid payment methods.\n\nThese changes aim to improve the robustness and flexibility of the payment processing system, facilitating better data handling and integrity.\n\n* Refactor payment schema to enhance data integrity and structure\n\n- Updated the ''payment'' table schema across MySQL, PostgreSQL, SQLite, and SQL Server to include an ''external_id'' field for better identification.\n- Modified the SQL insert statements to incorporate ''external_id'', ''billing_address_id'', ''method'', ''amount'', ''currency_code'', and ''status'' fields, improving the relational mapping and data management.\n- Added a check constraint for the ''method'' field to ensure valid payment methods.\n\nThese changes aim to improve the robustness and flexibility of the payment processing system, facilitating better data handling and integrity.\n\n* Enhance data integrity and structure in database schemas\n\n- Updated the ''account'', ''address'', and ''notification'' tables across MySQL, PostgreSQL, SQLite, and SQL Server to include ''external_id'' and ''tenant'' fields for better identification and multi-tenancy support.\n- Added check constraints for ''account_type'', ''currency_code'', and ''country'' fields to ensure valid values, improving data integrity.\n- Modified SQL insert statements to incorporate new fields, enhancing relational mapping and data management.\n\nThese changes aim to improve the robustness and flexibility of the database structure, facilitating better data handling and integrity.\n\n* Refactor account and address schemas for improved data integrity and structure\n\n- Updated the ''account'' table schema across MySQL, PostgreSQL, SQLite, and SQL Server to replace ''account_type'' and ''currency_code'' with a ''status'' field, enhancing clarity on account states.\n- Introduced new ''country'', ''state'', and ''city'' tables to normalize address data, establishing foreign key relationships in the ''address'' table.\n- Modified SQL insert statements to align with the new schema, ensuring accurate data representation and relational integrity.\n- Removed obsolete ''company'' table and related SQL scripts to streamline the database structure.\n\nThese changes aim to enhance the robustness and flexibility of the database, facilitating better data management and integrity.\n\n* Update database schemas and mock scripts for enhanced integration and consistency\n\n- Renamed schema files and updated paths in the E2E generator mock scripts to reflect the new naming conventions for database schemas.\n- Enhanced the DATA_DICTIONARY.md to include additional details on the new currency and payment_type tables, improving clarity on data relationships.\n- Updated SQL scripts for MySQL, PostgreSQL, and SQL Server to align with the new schema structure, ensuring consistency across different database types.\n- Added new tables for Gmail and Google Drive integrations, including necessary fields for multi-tenancy and data management.\n\nThese changes aim to improve the overall structure and usability of the database schemas, facilitating better integration and data handling across the application.","tree":{"sha":"e3d892b40f85ddb62d384b41c5846119f3825d10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Malnati/node-gen/git/trees/e3d892b40f85ddb62d384b41c5846119f3825d10"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Malnati/node-gen/git/commits/325c937f944b6db27ef9eb82791e909607590f4b","verification":{"payload":"tree e3d892b40f85ddb62d384b41c5846119f3825d10\nparent 57dcb6243939353632e46bf8bb0f6af4f09756d3\nauthor Ricardo Malnati <35036961+Malnati@users.noreply.github.com> 1771613348 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1771613348 -0300\n\nEnhance E2E testing setup with improved database support and document… (#207)\n\n* Enhance E2E testing setup with improved database support and documentation updates\n\n- Updated Docker Compose configuration to include additional database types and health checks, enhancing testing versatility.\n- Refactored E2E generator mock script to improve database connectivity checks and streamline testing processes.\n- Revised documentation to clarify new setup instructions and database connection handling, ensuring better usability for developers.\n\nThese changes aim to improve the robustness and flexibility of the E2E testing framework for the code generator.\n\n* Enhance database schema for accounts, addresses, contacts, payments, and users\n\n- Added ''tenant'' and ''account_id'' fields to the ''account'', ''address'', ''contact'', ''payment_method'', and ''app_user'' tables across MySQL, PostgreSQL, SQLite, and SQL Server schemas.\n- Updated corresponding SQL insert statements to include ''tenant'' and ''account_id'' for data consistency and relational integrity.\n\nThese changes aim to improve the structure and relational mapping of the database,