thService to verify database connectivity in production environments.\n- Updated the Docker Compose configuration to reflect changes in environment variables and service dependencies, ensuring proper initialization of all database services.\n\nThese changes aim to improve the robustness and versatility of the E2E testing framework, facilitating better testing across multiple database types.\n\n* Remove obsolete Docker Compose files and related database initialization scripts\n\n- Deleted `docker-compose.e2e.yml` and `docker-compose.yml` as part of the project restructuring to streamline the testing setup.\n- Removed associated SQL initialization scripts for MySQL and PostgreSQL to enhance clarity and organization in the database management.\n- Updated the Makefile to reflect changes in Docker Compose commands and paths, ensuring consistency with the new project structure.\n- Revised documentation to clarify the new setup and usage instructions for the remaining Docker configurations.\n\nThese changes aim to improve project organization and simplify the E2E testing framework.\n\n* Enhance TypeORM entity generation and E2E testing setup\n\n- Updated the TypeORMEntityGenerator to conditionally include column length options based on the data type, improving the accuracy of generated entity definitions.\n- Refactored the DataSourceService to implement the OnModuleInit interface, ensuring the data source is initialized when the module is loaded.\n- Modified the datasource template to reflect the changes in the DataSourceService, enhancing consistency across generated files.\n- Added a new function in the E2E generator mock script to check the reachability of database containers, improving the reliability of E2E tests.\n- Removed obsolete PostgreSQL initialization script to streamline the testing setup.\n\nThese changes aim to improve the robustness and flexibility of the entity generation and E2E testing framework.\n\n* Remove obsolete PostgreSQL initialization script to streamline E2E testing setup\n\n* Update PostgreSQL initialization script path and enhance documentation\n\n- Moved the PostgreSQL initialization script to a new directory structure under `test/e2e-generator-mock/pg-init/scripts/` to improve organization.\n- Updated the Docker Compose configuration to reflect the new script path, ensuring proper initialization during E2E tests.\n- Revised documentation in `README.md` files to clarify the new script location and its role in the E2E testing setup.\n\nThese changes aim to streamline the E2E testing process and enhance clarity in the project''s structure.","tree":{"sha":"996955ff6ad6329cd03837679cb6a57838043496","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Malnati/node-gen/git/trees/996955ff6ad6329cd03837679cb6a57838043496"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Malnati/node-gen/git/commits/65923a36d07874deb0739205e368c825c7f4061c","verification":{"payload":"tree 996955ff6ad6329cd03837679cb6a57838043496\nparent 5cda16257b4d52d6d53dc6f73ac3d9999753c842\nauthor Ricardo Malnati <35036961+Malnati@users.noreply.github.com> 1771472535 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1771472535 -0300\n\nFix/gen health e2e (#205)\n\n* Enhance E2E testing setup and database support\n\n- Updated the entrypoint script to include additional database types (Postgres, MySQL, SQL Server) in the E2E tests, improving flexibility in testing configurations.\n- Adjusted the sleep duration in readiness checks for databases from 2 seconds to 1.5 seconds to optimize the waiting time.\n- Refactored the package.json generator to dynamically include dependencies based on the selected database type, streamlining the setup process.\n- Enhanced the health check mechanism in the HealthService to verify database connectivity in production environments.\n- Updated the Docker Compose configuration to reflect changes in environment variables and service dependencies, ensuring proper initialization of all database services.\n\nThese changes aim to improve the robustness and versatility of the E2E testing framework, facilitating better testing across multiple database types.\n\n* Remove obsolete Docker Compose files and related database initialization scripts\n\n- Deleted `docker-compose.e2e.yml` and `docker-compose.yml` as part of the project restructuring to streamline the testing setup.\n- Removed associated SQL initialization scripts for MySQL and PostgreSQL to enhance clarity and organization in the database management.\n- Updated the Makefile to reflect changes in Docker Compose commands and paths, ensuring consistency with the new project structure.\n- Revised documentation to clarify the new setup and usage instructions for the remaining Docker configurations.\n\nThese changes aim to improve project organization and simplify the E2E testing framework.\n\n* Enhance TypeORM entity generation and E2E testing setup\n\n- Updated the TypeORMEntityGenerator to conditionally include column length options based on the data type, improving the accuracy of generated entity definitions.\n- Refactored the DataSourceService to implement the OnModuleInit interface, ensuring the data source is initialized when the module is loaded.\n- Modified the datasource template to reflect the changes in the DataSourceService, enhancing consistency across generated files.\n- Added a new function in the E2E generator mock script to check the reachability of database containers, improving the reliability of E2E tests.\n- Removed obsolete PostgreSQL initialization script to streamline the testing setup.\n\nThese changes aim to improve the robustness and flexibility of the entity generation and E2E testing framework.\n\n* Remove obsolete PostgreSQL initialization script to streamline E2E testing setup\n\n* Update PostgreSQL initialization script path and enhance documentation\n\n- Moved the PostgreSQL initialization script to a new directory structure under `test/e2e-generator-mock/pg-init/scripts/` to improve organization.\n- Updated the Docker Compose 