22:51:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix/env docker stack (#204)\n\n* Update .gitignore to enhance project structure and organization\n\n- Added entries for various environment files and logs to prevent them from being tracked.\n- Updated paths for build outputs and generated entities to reflect the new project structure.\n- Included additional cache and temporary files to improve build efficiency.\n- Removed obsolete entries and consolidated similar patterns for clarity.\n\nThese changes aim to streamline the project''s file management and improve clarity for developers.\n\n* Enhance Makefile with E2E testing support and improve command formatting\n\n- Updated the Makefile to include new targets for end-to-end (E2E) testing: `e2e-build`, `e2e-run`, and `e2e`.\n- Improved command formatting by removing unnecessary `@` symbols for echo commands, ensuring consistent indentation.\n- Added instructions in the README for executing E2E tests via Docker, clarifying the usage of `docker-compose.e2e.yml` and the associated Dockerfile.\n\nThese changes aim to streamline the testing process and enhance documentation for better developer experience.\n\n* Fix Makefile command for E2E testing by updating docker-compose syntax\n\n- Changed the command for E2E builds in the Makefile from `docker compose` to `docker-compose` for consistency with standard usage.\n- This adjustment aims to improve command reliability and maintain alignment with common Docker practices.\n\n* Enhance controller and service generation with external ID support\n\n- Updated the ControllerGenerator to include logic for handling entities with external IDs, allowing for dynamic route generation based on the presence of an external ID or primary key.\n- Modified the ServiceGenerator to adapt methods for finding, updating, and deleting entities based on either external ID or primary key, improving flexibility in service operations.\n- Adjusted templates for controllers and services to reflect these changes, ensuring that generated code accurately represents the new logic.\n- Updated the ConfigUtil to change the static directory for templates, enhancing clarity in file organization.\n\nThese enhancements aim to improve the generator''s capability to handle various entity configurations, streamlining the development process.\n\n* Refactor E2E generator mock script to improve build process\n\n- Updated the `assessResults` function in `run.js` to first run `npm install` with `--legacy-peer-deps` before executing the build command.\n- Increased the timeout for the install command from 120 seconds to 180 seconds to accommodate longer installation times.\n- Enhanced error handling to ensure that the build process only proceeds if the installation is successful, improving reliability in the E2E testing workflow.\n\nThese changes aim to streamline the build process and enhance the robustness of the E2E testing setup.\n\n* Refactor SQLite fixture creation for CLI tests\n\n- Replaced the path for the SQLite fixture creation script from `scripts/create-sqlite-fixture.js` to `test/mock/create-sqlite-fixture.js` in the documentation and execution plans.\n- Deleted the obsolete `create-sqlite-fixture.js` script, streamlining the project structure.\n- Updated references in the documentation to reflect the new script location and usage for CLI testing.\n\nThese changes enhance clarity and organization in the testing setup for SQLite.\n\n* Refactor mock database structure and update references\n\n- Moved SQLite mock database scripts and connection details from `test/mock/` to `test/e2e-generator-mock/`, enhancing project organization.\n- Updated documentation to reflect the new paths for mock database creation and usage in tests.\n- Removed obsolete files related to the old mock structure, streamlining the testing setup.\n\nThese changes aim to improve clarity and maintainability of the testing framework for the code generator.\n\n* Update output directory references and enhance Docker configuration\n\n- Changed the output directory from `test/e2e-generator-mock/out` to `output/` in various files, including `.dockerignore`, `.gitignore`, and documentation, to standardize output paths.\n- Updated the Docker Compose configuration to mount the new output directory, ensuring generated files are accessible.\n- Modified the entrypoint script to reflect the new path for the database creation script, improving clarity in the E2E testing workflow.\n\nThese changes aim to streamline the testing process and enhance project organization.\n\n* Refactor output directory structure and update documentation\n\n- Removed references to the obsolete `test/build-cli-test` directory in `.dockerignore`, `.gitignore`, and various documentation files, consolidating output paths to the `output/` directory.\n- Updated documentation to clarify the new output directory for generated files and SQLite fixture creation, enhancing clarity for users.\n- Deleted the now-unnecessary `test/build-cli-test` directory and its associated files, streamlining the project structure.\n\nThese changes aim to improve project organization and simplify the testing workflow.\n\n* Refactor database structure and update references for testing\n\n- Moved database scripts and related files from `test/db/` to `test/e2e-generator-mock/projects/user/db/`, enhancing project organization.\n- Updated paths in various scripts and configuration files to reflect the new database structure, ensuring consistency across the project.\n- Removed obsolete database files and updated documentation to clarify the new structure and usage for testing.\n\nThese changes aim to streamline the testing process and improve clarity in the project''s database management.\n\n* Refactor database structure for todo project and update references\n\n- Moved database scripts from `test/e2e-generator-mock/projects/user/db/` to `test/e2e-generator-mock/projects/todo/db/`, enhancing project organization.\n- Updated paths in various scripts, configuration files, and documentation to reflect the new database structure for the todo project.\n- Removed obsolete database files related to the user project, streamlining the testing setup.\n\nThese changes aim to improve clarity and maintainability of the testing framework for the code generator.\n\n* Enhance E2E testing setup and update documentation\n\n- Updated the entrypoint script to set the default database type to SQLite for E2E tests, improving configuration clarity.\n- Revised the README files to reflect the new database connection structure, detailing the use of separate connection files for different database types.\n- Removed the obsolete `connection.json` file, streamlining the connection management process.\n- Adjusted the E2E generator script to dynamically discover connection files and handle multiple database types, enhancing flexibility in testing.\n\nThese changes aim to improve the organization and clarity of the E2E testing framework for the code generator.\n\n* Remove obsolete Bitbucket Pipelines configuration file\n\n- Deleted the `bitbucket-pipelines.yml` file, which contained CI/CD configurations for the project. This removal streamlines the repository by eliminating outdated and unused configurations, enhancing overall project organization.\n\n* Enhance E2E testing setup with PostgreSQL support and update documentation\n\n- Added PostgreSQL service configuration to `docker-compose.e2e.yml`, including health checks and initialization scripts for the mock database.\n- Updated the E2E generator script to support multiple database types, allowing for both SQLite and PostgreSQL connections.\n- Revised README files to reflect changes in output directory structure and clarify the usage of multiple database types in E2E tests.\n\nThese updates aim to improve the flexibility and clarity of the E2E testing framework for the code generator.\n\n* Add SQL Server support to E2E testing setup and update documentation\n\n- Introduced SQL Server service configuration in `docker-compose.e2e.yml`, including environment variables and health checks.\n- Enhanced the entrypoint script to wait for SQL Server readiness and initialize the database schema.\n- Updated the E2E generator script to support SQL Server connections alongside existing SQLite and PostgreSQL options.\n- Revised README to include instructions for using SQL Server in E2E tests, clarifying the setup process and database types.\n\nThese changes aim to improve the flexibility and comprehensiveness of the E2E testing framework for the code generator.\n\n* Add MySQL support to E2E testing setup and update documentation\n\n- Introduced MySQL service configuration in `docker-compose.e2e.yml`, including environment variables and health checks.\n- Enhanced the entrypoint script to wait for MySQL readiness before proceeding with tests.\n- Updated the E2E generator script to support MySQL connections alongside existing database options.\n- Revised README to reflect the inclusion of MySQL in the E2E testing framework, clarifying the setup process and available database types.\n\nThese changes aim to improve the flexibility and comprehensiveness of the E2E testing framework for the code generator.\n\n* Enhance E2E testing setup with MongoDB support and update documentation\n\n- Introduced MongoDB service configuration in `docker-compose.e2e.yml`, including environment variables and health checks.\n- Enhanced the entrypoint script to wait for MongoDB readiness before proceeding with tests.\n- Updated the E2E generator script to support MongoDB connections alongside existing database options.\n- Revised README to reflect the inclusion of MongoDB in the E2E testing framework, clarifying the setup process and available database types.\n\nThese changes aim to improve the flexibility and comprehensiveness of the E2E testing framework for the code generator.\n\n* Enhance E2E testing setup with additional database initialization and relation handling\n\n- Updated `docker-compose.e2e.yml` to include new SQL initialization scripts for selling and schedule projects.\n- Enhanced the entrypoint script to wait for PostgreSQL readiness and initialize related mock databases as needed.\n- Improved DTO and service generation logic to handle foreign keys with external IDs, ensuring accurate relation mapping.\n- Refactored the E2E generator to support multiple projects with distinct database schemas, improving flexibility in testing.\n\nThese changes aim to enhance the robustness and versatility of the E2E testing framework for the code generator.\n\n* Enhance E2E testing setup with support for additional database types and update documentation\n\n- Updated `docker-compose.e2e.yml` to include configurations for new database services, enhancing testing versatility.\n- Improved entrypoint script to ensure readiness checks for all supported databases before executing tests.\n- Enhanced E2E generator script to accommodate connections for newly added databases alongside existing options.\n- Revised README to reflect the latest changes in database support and clarify setup instructions.\n\nThese updates aim to further improve the flexibility and comprehensiveness of the E2E testing framework for the code generator.","tree":{"sha":"f243cef224b2a70626ce2eb4e97b84053350f983","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Malnati/node-gen/git/trees/f243cef224b2a70626ce2eb4e97b84053350f983"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Malnati/node-gen/git/commits/5cda16257b4d52d6d53dc6f73ac3d9999753c842","verification":{"payload":"tree f243cef224b2a70626ce2eb4e97b84053350f983\nparent 459c3eaa1e06a3c3f39ae752df09c33e4b99e0ea\nauthor Ricardo Malnati <35036961+Malnati@users.noreply.github.com> 1771455068 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1771455068 -0300\n\nFix/env docker stack (#204)\n\n* Update .gitignore to enhance project structure and organization\n\n- Added entries for various environment files and logs to prevent them from be