e E2E generator script to support SQL Server connections alongside existing SQLite and PostgreSQL options.\n- Revised README to include instructions for using SQL Server in E2E tests, clarifying the setup process and database types.\n\nThese changes aim to improve the flexibility and comprehensiveness of the E2E testing framework for the code generator.\n\n* Add MySQL support to E2E testing setup and update documentation\n\n- Introduced MySQL service configuration in `docker-compose.e2e.yml`, including environment variables and health checks.\n- Enhanced the entrypoint script to wait for MySQL readiness before proceeding with tests.\n- Updated the E2E generator script to support MySQL connections alongside existing database options.\n- Revised README to reflect the inclusion of MySQL in the E2E testing framework, clarifying the setup process and available database types.\n\nThese changes aim to improve the flexibility and comprehensiveness of the E2E testing framework for the code generator.\n\n* Enhance E2E testing setup with MongoDB support and update documentation\n\n- Introduced MongoDB service configuration in `docker-compose.e2e.yml`, including environment variables and health checks.\n- Enhanced the entrypoint script to wait for MongoDB readiness before proceeding with tests.\n- Updated the E2E generator script to support MongoDB connections alongside existing database options.\n- Revised README to reflect the inclusion of MongoDB in the E2E testing framework, clarifying the setup process and available database types.\n\nThese changes aim to improve the flexibility and comprehensiveness of the E2E testing framework for the code generator.\n\n* Enhance E2E testing setup with additional database initialization and relation handling\n\n- Updated `docker-compose.e2e.yml` to include new SQL initialization scripts for selling and schedule projects.\n- Enhanced the entrypoint script to wait for PostgreSQL readiness and initialize related mock databases as needed.\n-