{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Malnati/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Malnati","id":35036961,"login":"Malnati","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MDM2OTYx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Malnati/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Malnati/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Malnati/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Malnati/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Malnati/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Malnati","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Malnati/node-gen/commits/dca70249043a7cf3d67eb4a1171146aabd93bee4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-18T03:11:12Z","email":"35036961+Malnati@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ricardo Malnati"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-18T03:11:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: enhance issue templates for generator review and execution plans (#199)\n\n* docs: enhance issue templates for generator review and execution plans\n\n* docs: update generator review plan with SUBs linkage and execution records\n\n- Added a section for linking SUBs in the EPIC document, detailing each SUB''s artifact and description.\n- Enhanced the execution plan documentation to include individual execution records for each SUB.\n- Updated the status tracking for the execution of commands and compliance with the review plan.\n\n* docs: update CLI configuration options for database types and components\n\n- Modified the database type option to include ''sqlite'' and ''sqlserver''.\n- Expanded the components option to allow for additional generation options, including ''diagram''.\n- Updated documentation to reflect successful CLI tests with SQLite.\n\n* docs: update CLI test execution plan with SQLite configuration details\n\n- Enhanced the documentation for executing CLI tests with SQLite, specifying the need for `-T ./static` to include `tsconfig.json` for successful compilation.\n- Updated the execution plan to reflect the outcomes of CLI commands and the presence of generated artifacts.\n- Clarified the requirements for in-memory SQLite usage and the implications for schema creation.\n\n* docs: update mock project structure and documentation\n\n- Revised the proposed directory structure for the mock project to use a `mock/` directory at the root of the repository instead of `fixtures/mock-codegen/` or `db/mock-codegen/`.\n- Updated documentation to reflect the new location for DDL and SQLite creation scripts, ensuring clarity on how to set up and use the mock project for testing.\n- Adjusted task checklist to align with the new directory structure.\n\n* docs: refine mock project documentation and execution guidelines\n\n- Updated the mock project documentation to clarify the new directory structure and its implications for testing.\n- Enhanced execution guidelines for CLI tests, including specific instructions for SQLite configuration and artifact generation.\n- Improved clarity on the requirements for using in-memory SQLite and schema creation processes.\n\n* docs: enhance mock project documentation and test automation references\n\n- Updated the documentation for CLI test execution to include a reference for automating the testing flow with the new project generator.\n- Added links to related documents for better traceability and context regarding the mock project and its integration with the CLI.\n- Clarified instructions for updating related documentation upon implementing the mock or executing tests.\n\n* docs: update mock project documentation for improved clarity and execution guidelines\n\n- Revised documentation to enhance clarity on the mock project structure and testing procedures.\n- Updated execution guidelines for CLI tests, including specific instructions for SQLite configuration.\n- Improved references to related documents for better context and traceability.\n\n* docs: update README and run script for enhanced validation of generated artifacts\n\n- Revised the README to clarify the assessment process for generated artifacts, including mandatory and optional checks.\n- Updated the run script to implement a detailed validation function that checks for the existence and correctness of generated files and directories.\n- Improved logging to provide clearer feedback on the validation results, including success and failure messages for each check.\n\n* docs: enhance README and run script for mock database connection handling\n\n- Updated the README to include details about the new `connection.json` file for mock database connection parameters.\n- Modified the run script to load connection details from `connection.json`, improving flexibility and eliminating hardcoded values.\n- Enhanced logging to provide clearer feedback on the mock database connection parameters used during execution.\n\n* docs: update README and mock project files for improved clarity and structure\n\n- Revised the README to reflect changes in application configuration, including updated app and database parameters.\n- Enhanced the mock project documentation to include new data model details, covering N-1 and N-N relationships.\n- Updated SQL schema to incorporate additional tables and relationships, improving the mock database structure.\n- Modified environment generator to allow for dynamic session endpoint configuration.\n\n* Potential fix for code scanning alert no. 12: Incomplete string escaping or encoding\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot Autofix powered by AI <62310815+github-advanced-security[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nSigned-off-by: Ricardo Malnati <35036961+Malnati@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Ricardo Malnati <35036961+Malnati@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Copilot Autofix powered by AI <62310815+github-advanced-security[bot]@users.noreply.githu